<!--
  SET YOUR DOMAIN: replace https://righttorecall.org throughout before launch.
  The same placeholder is in public/robots.txt and public/index.html.

  Only static routes are listed. Everything content-managed is discovered by
  crawling its index page rather than being hardcoded here, otherwise this file
  goes stale on every publish:

    /blog/:id                content-managed posts
    /campaigns/:id           content-managed campaigns
    /constitution/:number    constitution articles (crawled from /constitution)
    /representatives/:slug   profiles (crawled from /representatives)
    /states/:slug            36 state pages (crawled from /states)
    /petitions/:slug, /promises/:slug, /reports/:slug, /forum/:slug
    /academy/:slug, /research, /events/:slug

  KNOWN LIMITATION: this app is a client-rendered SPA, so a crawler that does not
  execute JavaScript sees an empty shell on every one of these routes and the
  index pages give it nothing to follow. That is the SEO problem §3 of
  IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md identifies, and the Next.js migration is its fix. Until
  then this sitemap tells a crawler the routes exist; it cannot make their
  content visible.
-->
